From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:03:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] ruffle_sdl: run with SDL 2.0.10

The sdl2 crate references SDL_Metal_DestroyView (SDL 2.0.12+, macOS Metal views), which ruffle_sdl never
calls. Linked with immediate binding, that one missing symbol kept the binary from starting on SDL 2.0.10
(Ubuntu 20.04, older firmwares); it is the only one of ruffle_sdl's 26 SDL imports that 2.0.10 lacks.
ruffle_sdl now defines it as a no-op, so it links and runs against SDL 2.0.10 and newer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sdl/src/main.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdl/src/main.rs b/sdl/src/main.rs
index 60b52912..b2148558 100644
--- a/sdl/src/main.rs
+++ b/sdl/src/main.rs
@@ -283,6 +283,13 @@ impl FsCommandProvider for FsCommands {
     }
 }
 
+/// SDL 2.0.10 compatibility: the sdl2 crate links `SDL_Metal_DestroyView` (added in SDL 2.0.12, macOS
+/// only), which ruffle_sdl never calls. Defining it here lets the binary link and start against SDL 2.0.10
+/// (Ubuntu 20.04, older firmwares); with a newer SDL this definition is used instead of the library's
+/// no-op Linux one, which changes nothing.
+#[unsafe(no_mangle)]
+pub extern "C" fn SDL_Metal_DestroyView(_view: *mut std::ffi::c_void) {}
+
